\ FASSEM.SEQ   Floating point assembler extensions      F-PC native port

comment:

  This file added the 8087/80287 instructions (FADD, FLD, FSTP, ST(i),
REAL*8 and so on) to the 8086 assembler, plus a few CODE words that read
and set the 8087 (>FREGS >FREGS> INITFP FPCW> >FPCW (F@) FPSW>, the (TAG)
and {.} helpers, and the (POWER) routine).

  Native port: there is no 8086 assembler and no 8087. CODE words are
written for the VM's abstract machine with the assembler in SRC/AMASM.SEQ
(already in the image; see its header for the instructions), and floating
point is a set of VM built-ins on a separate float stack of IEEE doubles
(F+ F- F* F/ FSQRT F** and the rest, see vm/prims.def). There is nothing
for an 8087 assembler to do, so this file defines nothing.

  The 8087 control and status words that FFLOAT.SEQ and FLTAUX.SEQ read
(FPCW> >FPCW FPSW> INITFP {.} (TAG)) are emulated in FFLOAT.SEQ itself.

comment;
